{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.9,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C7", "R5", "U1"],
      "pins": ["C7.1", "C7.2", "R5.1", "R5.2", "U1.8"],
      "nets": ["Net-(U1-EN{slash}CHIP_PU)", "GND", "+3V3"],
      "observed": "C7 is listed as a 10 mF capacitor in an 0805 footprint and is connected from the ESP32-C3 EN/CHIP_PU pin to GND, with R5 = 10 kΩ pulling EN to +3V3. The SPICE deck also models it as 10 m.",
      "expected": "The EN timing capacitor should be a microfarad-scale value, e.g. 1 µF or 10 µF, compatible with an 0805 ceramic and the shared LCSC code C15850 used by the 10 µF capacitors. 10 mF is not a realistic value for this role and would create an approximately 100 s RC time constant with 10 kΩ.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C7\") (value \"10mF\") (footprint \"Capacitor_SMD:C_0805_2012Metric\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"26\") (name \"Net-(U1-EN{slash}CHIP_PU)\") (node (ref \"C7\") (pin \"1\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R5\") (value \"10K\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C7 Net-_U1-EN/CHIP_PU_ 0 10m"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "With 10 mF and 10 kΩ, the MCU EN pin charges very slowly, holding the ESP32 in reset for many seconds or minutes and likely preventing normal boot. If the intended part is the 10 µF indicated by the LCSC code, the schematic value is a serious mislabel or sourcing error.",
      "confidence": 0.92
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most major interfaces match the specification, but the ESP32 enable capacitor C7 is specified as 10 mF in an 0805 package, which is inconsistent with its role and would prevent normal boot; this is the anomaly."
}

